---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { url } from '../utils/url';
---

<Layout title="Pricing" description="Inbind is free to download and use. Local-first markdown editor with AI editing built in.">
  <Header />

  <section class="mk-section" style="padding-top: 88px;">
    <div class="mk-container">
      <div class="mk-section-head">
        <div class="mk-section-eyebrow">Pricing</div>
        <h2 class="mk-section-h">Free. No strings.</h2>
        <p class="mk-section-sub">The full editor is free to download and use. We may introduce a paid plan down the line, but we'll be honest about what it is and who it's for when we do.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="mk-pricing-grid">
        <!-- Free -->
        <div class="mk-price-card">
          <h3>Free</h3>
          <div class="mk-price">
            <span class="mk-price-amt">$0</span>
            <span class="mk-price-per">/ forever</span>
          </div>
          <p style="color: var(--text-subtle); margin: 0; font-size: 14.5px;">The full editor. Local-only. Uses your Claude Code or Codex subscription for AI.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <svg class="mk-price-check" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                <polyline points="2 8 6 12 14 4"/>
              </svg>
              Real-time markdown editor
            </li>
            <li>
              <svg class="mk-price-check" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                <polyline points="2 8 6 12 14 4"/>
              </svg>
              Folder-based file browser with page properties
            </li>
            <li>
              <svg class="mk-price-check" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                <polyline points="2 8 6 12 14 4"/>
              </svg>
              AI chat with visual edit approval
            </li>
            <li>
              <svg class="mk-price-check" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                <polyline points="2 8 6 12 14 4"/>
              </svg>
              Works with your Claude Code or Codex subscription
            </li>
          </ul>
          <a class="mk-btn mk-btn--ghost" href={url('download')} style="margin-top: auto;">Download free</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- FAQ -->
      <div style="max-width: 720px; margin: 72px auto 0;">
        <h3 style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 24px; font-weight: 600; margin: 0 0 24px; letter-spacing: -0.02em; text-align: center;">A few honest answers</h3>

        <details class="mk-faq-item">
          <summary>Is Inbind really free?</summary>
          <p class="mk-faq-body">Yes. Download it, use it, keep your files. It uses your existing Claude Code or Codex subscription for AI, no separate setup needed.</p>
        </details>

        <details class="mk-faq-item">
          <summary>Will there ever be a paid plan?</summary>
          <p class="mk-faq-body">Probably. We're still figuring out what that looks like and who it's actually for. We'll be upfront about it before it happens.</p>
        </details>

        <details class="mk-faq-item">
          <summary>Where do my notes live?</summary>
          <p class="mk-faq-body">In a folder on your computer. As <code>.md</code> files. We don't have a cloud. If you put that folder in iCloud or Dropbox, it'll sync there. Up to you.</p>
        </details>

        <details class="mk-faq-item">
          <summary>Do you train on my notes?</summary>
          <p class="mk-faq-body">No. We don't see them.</p>
        </details>

        <details class="mk-faq-item">
          <summary>What happens to my files if I stop using Inbind?</summary>
          <p class="mk-faq-body">Nothing. They're <code>.md</code> files in a folder. Open them in any other editor. We're not the kind of tool you have to migrate out of.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
